  {
    "id": "7694080935121161485",
    "url": "https://www.tiktok.com/@prep.momma/video/7694080935121161485",
    "author": "prep.momma",
    "author_followers": "3269",
    "caption": "When your toilet or sewer or septic system can\u2019t be used safely, a simple emergency bucket toilet can provide a temporary backup. \ud83d\udebd There are several ways to create a temporary sanitation setup. This is one straightforward option that can be adapted to the supplies available and the situation your household is facing. Store the basics before you need them: \u2022 A sturdy 5-gallon bucket \u2022 A split pool noodle for a makeshift seat \u2022 Heavy-duty contractor bags \u2022 Kitty litter or portable-toilet waste-gelling powder \u2022 A scoop, toilet paper and disposable gloves \u2022 Soap and safe handwashing water \u2022 An optional second bucket with a secure lid for containing tied waste bags Place the toilet bucket on a firm, level surface and secure the pool noodle around the rim. Double-line the bucket, add absorbent material and add more after each use. Keep it covered between uses, and tie the bags before they become too heavy. Store tied waste bags away from food, water, children and pets until local officials provide disposal instructions. Always wash your hands after handling the bucket or bags. Never add bleach or other household chemicals directly to human waste. It isn\u2019t a glamorous subject\u2014but safe sanitation is an important part of emergency preparedness. Small preparations now can protect your household\u2019s comfort, dignity and health later. \ud83e\uddfc #prepmomma #emergencytoilet #sanitation #wateroutage #temporarytoilet ",
